James expressed frustration with new OpenAI models not completing within the specified "max_completion_tokens" due to being verbose. He shared his usual API call format and noted that his system message asks for direct answers, which seems ineffective. I provided a comprehensive response outlining strategies to encourage concise outputs. Key suggestions included adding an explicit response contract with concrete limits, using model-native controls like setting "reasoning_effort" and "verbosity," decoupling output size from input length, instructing the model to prioritize important information first, and inspecting token usage to identify reasoning-token pressures. I recommended a practical default call format incorporating these guidelines, emphasizing clarity on expected response characteristics, and employing low verbosity and reasoning efforts where possible.
